  "title": "Ihr Kinderlein, kommet",
  "composer": "Johann Abraham Peter Schulz",
  "about": "Ihr Kinderlein, kommet means Come, little children in German. The priest Christoph von Schmid wrote the words around 1808 to 1810, and called his poem The Children at the Manger. Johann Abraham Peter Schulz wrote the tune in 1794 for a spring poem by Wilhelm Gottlieb Becker. The teacher Friedrich Hermann Eickhoff first set Schmid's words to it, and the song was first sung at Christmas 1829.",
  "funFact": "The same tune carries a summer song in Iceland, and an evening song in German-speaking Switzerland.",
